      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but it still feels a little bit like they're just trading cliches, you know? like 'liberal agenda' vs 'balanced education'. it's a bit too surface-level.\n\ncan u make it more visceral? i want the arguments to actually hit home. like, for David, can u make him bring up specific things he's worried about—maybe how this will affect the community's traditional values or how it feels like parents are being stripped of their right to guide their kids? \n\nand for Elena, instead of just saying 'it's about accuracy,' i want her to challenge him. i want her to point out that the 'traditional' way of teaching was actually just ignoring certain parts of history to make people more comfortable. make her sound like she's calling out the hypocrisy of his 'truth' being based on what's convenient.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
